Outline

Adding Comments and Standardizing Documentation

• Speaker 1 emphasizes the importance of adding comments to methods and specific actions in the application for future maintenance.

• Speaker 2 agrees with the feedback and Speaker 3 supports the idea of standard commenting at the file and method levels.

• Speaker 1 mentions the need for security scanning and standard processes for NuGet packages and libraries.

• Speaker 2 confirms that the application has undergone security scanning and that a request for the 1.17 version of the OpenTelemetry NuGet package has been made.

Performance Testing and Exception Handling

• Speaker 1 inquires about the performance impact of adding tracing to the application.

• Speaker 2 confirms that performance tests were run multiple times in test environments and regression tests, showing no significant overhead.

• Speaker 4 suggests removing unnecessary try-catch blocks if no action is taken on the exceptions.

• Speaker 2 explains the challenge of using different versions of the logger in various applications and the need to capture exceptions and log them appropriately.

Challenges with WCF Services and Instrumentation

• Speaker 2 discusses the unique challenges of instrumenting WCF services, including the need for propagation behavior and endpoint modifications.

• Speaker 2 explains the use of an app setting to enable or disable performance instrumentation without affecting existing service behavior.

• Speaker 3 outlines the principles followed for capturing data, ensuring it does not impact performance or functionality.

• Speaker 4 suggests creating a wiki page to document the different ways to consume the instrumentation package.

Future Plans and Application Scope

• Speaker 2 mentions that the current focus is on getting approval for performance instrumentation in the PA portal and monitoring its impact in production.

• Speaker 3 confirms that the next application to be instrumented is the eligibility verification service.

• Speaker 2 explains the priority order for instrumenting other applications based on their urgency and the need to monitor the current implementation before moving forward.

• Speaker 3 emphasizes the importance of stabilizing the current implementation in production before expanding to other applications.

Monitoring and Alerting

