• Speaker 2 explains that the current plan is to run reports to identify slow store procedures and services, but no real-time alerts are in place.

• Speaker 3 mentions the possibility of pushing data to Elasticsearch (ELK) for real-time monitoring and creating reports for performance analysis.

• Speaker 4 suggests using Dynatrace for real-time monitoring and reducing the lag between data collection and analysis.

Purge Process and Data Retention

• Speaker 4 raises the issue of the large amount of data being added to the database and the need for a purge process.

• Speaker 1 and Speaker 3 agree that a plan for data retention and purge should be developed based on the collected data.

• Speaker 2 mentions that the current focus is on reviewing the collected data to determine the criteria for data retention and purge.

• Speaker 3 confirms that the purge process will be determined based on the collected data and the need to manage the raw data effectively.

